=== TOPIC ===
id: aiml-ml-pipeline
title: Machine Learning Pipeline Sub-Roadmap
roadmapId: ai-ml-engineer
type: subroadmap
targetSubroadmap: machine-learning
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 110
summary: End-to-end data pipeline from raw ingestion and feature engineering to cross-validation and hyperparameter tuning.
explanation: Production machine learning requires a repeatable pipeline architecture: ingestion, validation, cleaning, feature scaling, encoding, model training, cross-validation, and artifact serialization. Pipelines eliminate data leakage between train and test distributions.
codeExample: # Conceptual scikit-learn Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\npipe = Pipeline([\n    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n    ('classifier', LogisticRegression())\n])\nprint("Pipeline defined:", pipe)
objective: Construct leak-free preprocessing pipelines using scikit-learn transformers
objective: Apply k-fold cross-validation and stratified sampling
objective: Tune hyperparameters systematically using grid search and Bayesian optimization
pitfall: Data leakage: fitting scalers or encoders on the entire dataset prior to train/test split
pitfall: Evaluating models on training data leading to unspotted overfitting
prerequisites: aiml-dsa-subroadmap
resource: Scikit-Learn Pipeline Documentation|https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/compose.html|documentation

