id: aiml-supervised-learning
title: Supervised Learning: Regression, Classification & Ensembles
roadmapId: ai-ml-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 80
summary: Linear regression, logistic regression, decision trees, random forests, and gradient boosted trees (XGBoost).
explanation: Supervised learning trains models on labeled datasets (features X mapping to target y). Linear and logistic models establish baseline relationships. Tree-based ensemble methods (Random Forest bagging, XGBoost/LightGBM gradient boosting) represent state-of-the-art architectures for tabular predictive tasks.
codeExample: # XGBoost Training Pattern\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n\nX_train = np.random.randn(100, 4)\ny_train = (X_train[:, 0] > 0).astype(int)\n\nclf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=10)\nclf.fit(X_train, y_train)\nprint("Predictions:", clf.predict(X_train[:3]))
objective: Train and evaluate linear and logistic regression models with regularization (L1/L2)
objective: Explain the bias-variance tradeoff and ensemble voting/boosting principles
objective: Train high-accuracy gradient boosted decision trees using XGBoost
pitfall: Overfitting trees by allowing unlimited depth on small datasets
pitfall: Failing to handle class imbalance resulting in misleading high accuracy scores
pitfall: Neglecting feature scaling for distance-based or linear models
prerequisites: aiml-ml-pipeline
resource: An Introduction to Statistical Learning (James et al.)|https://www.statlearning.com/|book

