id: aiml-model-evaluation-metrics
title: Model Evaluation, Validation & Drift Monitoring
roadmapId: ai-ml-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 60
summary: Precision, recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC, confusion matrices, data drift, and calibration.
explanation: Model evaluation requires selecting metrics aligned with domain business goals. For imbalanced datasets, raw accuracy is deceptive; precision, recall, PR curves, and ROC-AUC evaluate discrimination thresholds. Post-deployment, models must be monitored for covariate and concept drift.
codeExample: from sklearn.metrics import classification_report\n\ny_true = [0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 0]\ny_pred = [0, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1]\nprint(classification_report(y_true, y_pred, zero_division=0))
objective: Compute confusion matrices, precision, recall, and F1 metrics
objective: Plot and interpret ROC and Precision-Recall curves across decision thresholds
objective: Identify concept drift and dataset shift in production pipelines
pitfall: Evaluating models on imbalanced datasets using only accuracy
pitfall: Selecting classification thresholds arbitrarily at 0.5 without cost analysis
pitfall: Assuming static test set performance holds indefinitely in production
prerequisites: aiml-deep-learning-neural-nets
resource: Google Machine Learning Crash Course: Classification Metrics|https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/precision-and-recall|course

