id: fullstack-relational-nosql-db
title: Database Modeling for Web Apps: SQL vs NoSQL Document Stores
roadmapId: fullstack-developer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 75
summary: Comparing relational schemas (PostgreSQL) vs document databases (MongoDB), data modeling, and migrations.
explanation: Full-stack developers select storage architectures based on access patterns and relational complexity. Relational databases excel at structured transactions, referential integrity, and complex joins. Document stores (MongoDB) excel at hierarchical, semi-structured schemas and rapid prototyping.
codeExample: // Document Model Structure for Topic Progress\nconst userProgressDoc = {\n  userId: "usr_9981",\n  completedTopics: ["c-syntax-basics", "c-variables"],\n  currentRoadmap: "c",\n  updatedAt: new Date().toISOString()\n};
objective: Model application entities in relational schemas and document trees
objective: Execute repeatable schema migration scripts in production environments
objective: Select appropriate database engines based on query patterns and read/write ratios
pitfall: Choosing NoSQL document databases for deeply interconnected relational data
pitfall: Running un-versioned manual database updates directly in production databases
pitfall: Ignoring indexing on nested document fields in MongoDB
prerequisites: fullstack-api-security-cors
resource: PostgreSQL vs MongoDB: Architectural Comparison|https://www.postgresql.org/about/|documentation

