id: fullstack-cloud-deployment
title: Full-Stack Cloud Deployment, Static Hosting & CDN Edge
roadmapId: fullstack-developer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 80
summary: Static asset distribution via CDNs, cloud virtual machines, HTTPS certificates, reverse proxying, and DNS.
explanation: Modern web applications deploy static frontend bundles (HTML, CSS, JS) to global Content Delivery Networks (CDNs) for minimal edge latency, while backend APIs run on cloud compute instances or serverless containers. Reverse proxies coordinate domain routing, TLS encryption, and health checks.
codeExample: # Nginx Reverse Proxy & Static Host Configuration\n# server {\n#   listen 80;\n#   server_name pathforge.dev;\n#   root /var/www/pathforge/frontend;\n#   location /api/ {\n#     proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;\n#   }\n# }
