pitfall: Leaving development environment debug endpoints exposed to the public internet
pitfall: Failing to set up automated SSL certificate renewal
prerequisites: fullstack-relational-nosql-db
resource: Nginx Beginner's Guide|https://nginx.org/en/docs/beginners_guide.html|documentation


=== TOPIC ===
id: c-arrays-strings
title: Arrays, Strings & Bounds
roadmapId: c
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Work with contiguous arrays, character buffers, and explicit length tracking.
explanation: C arrays store elements contiguously and do not carry their own length at runtime. String conventions use a terminating '\0' byte, so callers must track buffer capacity and validate indexes. Array parameters are adjusted to pointers, which means functions generally need an explicit length argument.
codeExample: #include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    char name[16] = "PathForge";\n    printf("%zu characters\n", strlen(name));\n    return 0;\n}
objective: Declare and traverse arrays using valid index bounds
objective: Distinguish a character array's capacity from its string length
objective: Pass array data together with its length to functions
pitfall: Writing one element beyond the array boundary
pitfall: Using an uninitialized character buffer as a string
pitfall: Assuming an array parameter preserves its size
prerequisites: c-variables,c-control-flow
resource: C arrays|https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/language/array|documentation
resource: C string handling|https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/byte|documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: c-preprocessor-build
title: Headers, Macros & Build Organization
roadmapId: c
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner to Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Organize multi-file C programs with headers, declarations, macros, and compiler flags.
explanation: The preprocessor handles include directives and macro expansion before compilation. Header files expose declarations while source files contain definitions. Include guards prevent repeated inclusion, and a repeatable build command should enable warnings so interface and type errors are found early.
codeExample: #ifndef PATHFORGE_UTILS_H\n#define PATHFORGE_UTILS_H\nint clamp(int value, int low, int high);\n#endif
objective: Separate declarations from definitions across .h and .c files
objective: Use include guards and macros carefully
objective: Compile multiple translation units with useful warnings
pitfall: Defining non-inline functions in headers included by many files
pitfall: Using macros with side effects
pitfall: Ignoring compiler warnings
prerequisites: c-syntax-basics,c-functions
resource: GCC warning options|https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Warning-Options.html|documentation
resource: C language reference|https://en.cppreference.com/w/c|documentation

