id: java-generics-streams
title: Generics, Lambdas & Stream Processing
roadmapId: java
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Write reusable typed collections and transform data with functional operations.
explanation: Generics provide compile-time type constraints for classes and methods. Lambdas express behavior as values, and streams describe pipelines such as filtering, mapping, and aggregation. Streams are not storage containers; they process a source and should be used where the pipeline improves clarity.
codeExample: List<String> names = List.of("Ada", "Linus", "Grace");\nList<String> longNames = names.stream()\n    .filter(name -> name.length() > 4)\n    .toList();
