id: python-comprehensions-iterators
title: Comprehensions, Iterators & Generators
roadmapId: python
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Transform collections clearly and process large sequences lazily.
explanation: Comprehensions construct collections from iterables, while iterators expose values one at a time. Generator functions use yield to produce lazy sequences, reducing peak memory use for streaming workloads. Choose the simplest construct that makes the transformation understandable.
codeExample: def even_squares(values):\n    for value in values:\n        if value % 2 == 0:\n            yield value * value\n\nprint(list(even_squares(range(8))))
objective: Use list and dictionary comprehensions appropriately
objective: Explain the iterator protocol at a high level
objective: Use generators for lazy data processing
pitfall: Building large intermediate lists unnecessarily
pitfall: Writing deeply nested comprehensions that are hard to read
pitfall: Expecting an exhausted iterator to restart automatically
prerequisites: python-functions,python-data-structures
resource: Python Iterator Types|https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#iterator-types|documentation
resource: Python Generator Expressions|https://docs.python.org/3/howto/functional.html#generators|documentation

