id: aiml-data-cleaning-feature-engineering
title: Data Cleaning & Feature Engineering
roadmapId: ai-ml-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 80
summary: Inspect missing values, encode variables, scale features, and avoid data leakage.
explanation: Data preparation converts raw records into model-ready features. Missing-value strategies, categorical encoding, scaling, and train/test separation must be fitted using training data only where appropriate. Data leakage occurs when information unavailable at prediction time influences training or evaluation.
codeExample: from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n\npreprocess = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("numeric", StandardScaler(), numeric_columns),\n    ("categorical", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"), categorical_columns),\n])
objective: Identify missingness and outliers before selecting a treatment
objective: Build reproducible preprocessing pipelines
objective: Explain and prevent target leakage
pitfall: Fitting scalers or encoders on the full dataset before splitting
pitfall: Dropping missing rows without understanding the mechanism
pitfall: Using features that would not exist at prediction time
prerequisites: aiml-python-scientific-stack,aiml-ml-pipeline
resource: Scikit-learn Preprocessing|https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/preprocessing.html|documentation
resource: Google ML Data Preparation|https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/data-prep|course

