explanation: Unsupervised methods seek structure without a target label. Clustering methods such as k-means depend on distance and scaling choices, while dimensionality-reduction methods can support exploration and visualization. Results need domain interpretation rather than assuming clusters are objectively meaningful.
codeExample: from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nmodel = KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=42, n_init="auto")\nlabels = model.fit_predict(X_scaled)
