=== TOPIC ===
id: backend-rate-limiting
title: Rate Limiting & Resilience Patterns
roadmapId: backend-developer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 70
summary: Protect APIs and dependencies with quotas, timeouts, retries, and graceful degradation.
explanation: Rate limiting constrains request volume per identity or resource, while timeouts prevent work from waiting indefinitely. Retries should be bounded and normally use backoff with jitter; retrying non-idempotent operations can duplicate side effects. Circuit breakers and bulkheads can limit cascading failures.
codeExample: import time, random\n\ndef backoff(attempt):\n    ceiling = min(8.0, 0.5 * (2 ** attempt))\n    return random.uniform(0, ceiling)
objective: Choose rate-limit keys and response behavior
objective: Set bounded timeouts and retry budgets
objective: Explain idempotency and cascading failure
pitfall: Retrying forever during an outage
pitfall: Retrying non-idempotent operations without safeguards
pitfall: Applying one global quota to unrelated clients
prerequisites: backend-internet-protocols,backend-caching-redis
resource: Google SRE Book: Handling Overload|https://sre.google/sre-book/handling-overload/|book
resource: AWS Builders Library: Timeouts, retries, and backoff|https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/|article

