id: fullstack-accessibility
title: Semantic HTML & Accessibility
roadmapId: fullstack-developer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner to Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Build interfaces that support keyboard navigation, assistive technology, and meaningful document structure.
explanation: Semantic HTML communicates the role and structure of content to browsers and assistive technologies. Accessible controls need labels, keyboard operation, visible focus, and appropriate status announcements. Automated checks are useful but cannot replace manual keyboard and screen-reader testing.
codeExample: <label for="email">Email address</label>\n<input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
objective: Choose semantic elements based on purpose
objective: Provide labels and keyboard-accessible interactions
objective: Test focus order and error messaging
pitfall: Using clickable divs instead of native controls
pitfall: Removing focus outlines without a replacement
pitfall: Relying only on automated accessibility scores
prerequisites: fullstack-web-architecture,fullstack-dom-api
resource: MDN Accessibility|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility|documentation
resource: W3C WCAG Overview|https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/|standard

