id: fullstack-frontend-testing
title: Frontend Testing & Browser Debugging
roadmapId: fullstack-developer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Test component behavior and debug browser-side failures with repeatable checks.
explanation: Frontend tests should verify user-visible behavior, state transitions, validation, and error states. Browser developer tools help inspect DOM, network requests, storage, and runtime errors. Tests should avoid brittle assumptions about internal component implementation.
codeExample: // Example assertion style with a browser testing library\nexpect(screen.getByRole("button", { name: /save/i })).toBeEnabled();
objective: Test components through accessible roles and user actions
objective: Use browser tools to inspect network and runtime errors
objective: Cover loading, empty, success, and failure states
pitfall: Testing only implementation details
pitfall: Ignoring failed network requests
pitfall: Leaving flaky tests dependent on arbitrary delays
