type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 45
summary: Compare infrastructure, platform, and software services and identify which security responsibilities remain with the customer.
explanation: Cloud service models move different layers of operation to the provider. The exact shared-responsibility boundary depends on the service and configuration.
codeExample: 
objective: Compare IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS
objective: identify customer-controlled identities and data
objective: explain region and availability zone concepts.
pitfall: Assuming the provider secures application permissions and customer data automatically.
