roadmapId: database-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 75
summary: Translate business entities and relationships into tables with keys and constraints.
explanation: A relational model separates entities and relationships into relations. Normalization reduces update anomalies, while constraints encode data rules close to the stored data.
codeExample: 
objective: Design primary and foreign keys
objective: normalize common schemas
objective: define nullability and uniqueness rules.
pitfall: Duplicating facts across rows
pitfall: using application code as the only integrity check.
prerequisites: 
