type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 45
summary: Balance unit, integration, and end-to-end tests to obtain useful feedback at different costs.
explanation: Unit tests isolate small behavior, integration tests validate boundaries, and end-to-end tests exercise full workflows. The right balance depends on architecture and risk rather than a fixed universal ratio.
codeExample: 
objective: Select an appropriate test level
objective: isolate dependencies where useful
objective: minimize flaky tests.
pitfall: Using only end-to-end tests
pitfall: mocking away the behavior that needs verification.
