id: mleng-problem-framing
title: Frame an ML Problem
roadmapId: machine-learning-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 45
summary: Translate a business or scientific question into a measurable machine-learning task.
explanation: Define the prediction target, unit of analysis, decision context, baseline, and success metric before choosing an algorithm. Identify whether the task is classification, regression, ranking, clustering, or forecasting, and check whether a model is appropriate at all.
codeExample: 
objective: State the target and intended decision
objective: Choose a baseline and task-appropriate metric
objective: Identify leakage and data-availability risks
pitfall: Starting with a model before defining the target
pitfall: Using a metric unrelated to the real decision
prerequisites: 
resource: Scikit-learn: Choosing the right estimator|https://scikit-learn.org/stable/machine_learning_map.html|documentation
