=== TOPIC ===
id: aieng-structured-output
title: Structured Outputs and Validation
roadmapId: ai-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Turn model responses into validated application data rather than trusting free-form text.
explanation: Use constrained output formats or schemas where supported, then validate the returned object in application code. Schema compliance does not guarantee factual correctness or safe values; business rules and authorization still belong in deterministic code.
codeExample: from pydantic import BaseModel, Field

class TicketSummary(BaseModel):
    category: str
    priority: int = Field(ge=1, le=5)
    rationale: str

# Validate model output before using it in application logic.
objective: Define a response schema
objective: Validate semantic and business constraints
objective: Handle refusal, truncation, and invalid output
pitfall: Treating valid JSON as necessarily correct
pitfall: Using model-generated fields to bypass authorization
prerequisites: aieng-inference-api
resource: Pydantic documentation|https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/|documentation
resource: JSON Schema documentation|https://json-schema.org/learn/getting-started-step-by-step|documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: aieng-tool-use
title: Tool Use and Controlled Actions
roadmapId: ai-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Connect model reasoning to explicitly permitted tools while keeping execution under application control.
explanation: Expose narrow tool definitions, validate arguments, enforce user permissions, and require confirmation for consequential actions. Tool output is untrusted input. Separate proposing an action from executing it, and keep an audit trail for sensitive operations.
codeExample: 
objective: Define minimal tool schemas and permissions
objective: Validate tool arguments and outputs
objective: Gate high-impact actions behind confirmation
pitfall: Allowing arbitrary shell or database access
pitfall: Assuming a model-generated request is authorized
prerequisites: aieng-structured-output
resource: OWASP LLM Top 10|https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/|security reference
resource: LangChain tools concepts|https://python.langchain.com/docs/concepts/tools/|documentation

