id: aieng-security-cost
title: AI Security, Privacy, and Cost Controls
roadmapId: ai-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Reduce prompt-injection, data exposure, and runaway inference cost risks.
explanation: Treat retrieved documents and tool results as untrusted content. Apply least privilege, data minimization, output handling, per-user quotas, token limits, and cost monitoring. Red-team testing should include indirect prompt injection and unauthorized data-access attempts.
codeExample: 
objective: Apply least privilege to tools and data
objective: Set quotas and maximum input/output sizes
objective: Test prompt-injection and sensitive-data cases
pitfall: Relying on a system prompt as the only security boundary
pitfall: Logging API keys or full sensitive prompts
prerequisites: aieng-evaluation
resource: OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications|https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/|security reference
