roadmapId: llm-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Understand the practical constraints that shape large-language-model input and output.
explanation: Tokenization maps text to model tokens, not necessarily words. Context limits constrain combined instructions, conversation history, retrieved evidence, and generated output. Different tokenizers can produce different token counts for the same text.
codeExample: 
objective: Estimate token usage and context pressure
objective: Explain why chunking and summarization are needed
objective: Distinguish context length from model knowledge
pitfall: Assuming one token equals one word
pitfall: Filling the context with irrelevant history
