id: llme-prompt-design
title: Prompt Design and Instruction Hierarchy
roadmapId: llm-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Design prompts that state task, constraints, context, and output requirements clearly.
explanation: A robust prompt separates instructions from user-provided or retrieved data, defines the expected output, and includes representative examples when useful. Prompt changes should be versioned and evaluated rather than judged from a few subjective trials.
codeExample: 
objective: Write explicit task and output constraints
objective: Separate trusted instructions from untrusted content
objective: Version prompts and compare test results
pitfall: Assuming wording alone guarantees factual accuracy
pitfall: Mixing retrieved text into instructions without clear boundaries
