id: llme-embeddings-retrieval
title: Embeddings and Semantic Retrieval
roadmapId: llm-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 70
summary: Retrieve relevant passages using embeddings and a similarity index.
explanation: Embedding models represent text as vectors; nearest-neighbor search retrieves semantically similar items, but similarity is not the same as truth or relevance. Chunking, metadata filters, hybrid lexical/vector search, and reranking can improve retrieval depending on the corpus and task.
codeExample: 
objective: Create and index document chunks
objective: Compare keyword and vector retrieval
objective: Measure recall and relevance on labeled queries
pitfall: Choosing chunk sizes without evaluation
pitfall: Ignoring document permissions during retrieval
prerequisites: llme-prompt-design
resource: Sentence Transformers documentation|https://www.sbert.net/|documentation
resource: Qdrant documentation|https://qdrant.tech/documentation/|documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: llme-rag-pipeline
title: Retrieval-Augmented Generation Pipeline
roadmapId: llm-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 75
summary: Ground generated answers in retrieved evidence and expose the sources used.
explanation: A RAG pipeline ingests documents, extracts and chunks content, indexes it, retrieves passages for a query, and supplies selected evidence to a model. Evaluate retrieval and generation separately; provide citations only when the cited source actually supports the claim.
codeExample: documents = load_documents()
chunks = split_documents(documents)
index = build_vector_index(chunks)

def answer(question):
    evidence = index.search(question, k=5)
    return generate_answer(question, evidence), evidence
objective: Implement ingestion, retrieval, and generation stages
objective: Return source metadata with answers
objective: Test retrieval failures and unsupported questions
pitfall: Assuming RAG eliminates hallucinations
pitfall: Citing documents that were not used or do not support the answer
prerequisites: llme-embeddings-retrieval
resource: LlamaIndex documentation|https://docs.llamaindex.ai/|documentation
resource: LangChain retrieval concepts|https://python.langchain.com/docs/concepts/retrieval/|documentation

