summary: Measure answer quality, grounding, retrieval coverage, and failure rates.
explanation: Create a representative test set with expected answer properties and source evidence. Evaluate retrieval recall and ranking separately from answer correctness, groundedness, refusal behavior, and latency. Use human review for high-impact or subjective outputs.
codeExample: 
objective: Measure retrieval and generation separately
objective: Track unsupported-answer and citation errors
objective: Add regressions from real failures
pitfall: Using only a single aggregate LLM-as-judge score
pitfall: Testing on examples copied from the prompt only
