id: mlops-experiment-tracking
title: Experiment Tracking and Reproducibility
roadmapId: mlops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Compare experiments with recorded parameters, metrics, artifacts, and environment details.
explanation: An experiment tracker makes comparisons auditable and helps teams reproduce results. Log the evaluation protocol alongside metrics so a score cannot be detached from the split, data version, or code that produced it.
codeExample: import mlflow

with mlflow.start_run():
    mlflow.log_param("model", "baseline")
    mlflow.log_metric("validation_f1", validation_f1)
    mlflow.log_artifact("evaluation.json")
objective: Log parameters, metrics, and artifacts
objective: Compare runs using consistent evaluation data
objective: Capture code and environment metadata
pitfall: Comparing runs with inconsistent data splits
pitfall: Logging only the best run and losing failed experiments
prerequisites: mlops-data-versioning
resource: MLflow tracking quickstart|https://mlflow.org/docs/latest/ml/tracking/|documentation

