id: sre-error-budgets
title: Error Budgets and Reliability Trade-offs
roadmapId: site-reliability-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 45
summary: Use error budgets to balance release velocity and reliability goals.
explanation: An error budget is the tolerated unreliability implied by an SLO over its measurement window. Teams can use budget consumption to inform release risk, investment in reliability, and incident review, but policy must be agreed in advance.
codeExample: 
objective: Calculate a simple error budget
objective: Define a policy for rapid budget burn
objective: Explain the trade-off between availability and change rate
pitfall: Treating the budget as a target to consume
pitfall: Changing policy only after a high-profile incident
prerequisites: sre-sli-slo
