=== TOPIC ===
id: sre-telemetry
title: Metrics, Logs, Traces, and Alerting
roadmapId: site-reliability-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Use correlated telemetry to diagnose failures and detect user-impacting symptoms.
explanation: Metrics summarize behavior over time, logs record events, and traces connect work across distributed components. Alerts should be actionable and tied to user impact or imminent risk; high-cardinality labels can make telemetry expensive.
codeExample: http_requests_total{service="api",status="500"}

# Example PromQL: rate(http_requests_total{status=~"5.."}[5m])
objective: Choose telemetry for a debugging question
objective: Correlate trace and log context
objective: Write an actionable alert
pitfall: Alerting on every transient error
pitfall: Using unbounded user IDs as metric labels
prerequisites: sre-error-budgets
resource: Prometheus documentation|https://prometheus.io/docs/introduction/overview/|documentation
resource: OpenTelemetry documentation|https://opentelemetry.io/docs/|documentation

