=== TOPIC ===
id: sre-automation-toil
title: Operational Automation and Toil Reduction
roadmapId: site-reliability-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Automate repetitive operational work while preserving visibility and safe controls.
explanation: Toil is repetitive, manual operational work that scales with service growth and provides limited enduring value. Automations should be observable, permissioned, idempotent where possible, and have a manual recovery path.
codeExample: 
objective: Identify repeatable toil from incident data
objective: Automate a bounded workflow with audit logs
objective: Measure saved effort and failure rates
pitfall: Automating an unclear process before simplifying it
pitfall: Giving automation broader privileges than needed
prerequisites: sre-capacity-load
