id: net-models-addressing
title: Network Models, IP Addressing, and Subnetting
roadmapId: network-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 60
summary: Understand layered network communication and calculate IPv4 subnet ranges.
explanation: Layered models help separate link, network, transport, and application concerns. IPv4 CIDR prefixes determine network and host portions; IPv6 has different address conventions and should not be treated as IPv4 with longer strings.
codeExample: ip address show
ip route

# Windows equivalents for basic inspection: ipconfig /all and route print
objective: Explain encapsulation across network layers
objective: Calculate network and broadcast addresses for IPv4 subnets
objective: Read basic IPv6 notation
pitfall: Confusing a host address with a network prefix
pitfall: Assuming every network uses the same private address range
