id: net-switching-routing
title: Switching, Routing, and Network Paths
roadmapId: network-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Beginner
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Explain how local switching and IP routing move traffic between network segments.
explanation: Switches forward frames within a Layer 2 domain using learned MAC addresses; routers forward packets between IP networks using routing tables. Troubleshooting requires checking both the local path and the route to the destination.
codeExample: 
objective: Differentiate switching and routing
objective: Read a simple routing table
objective: Trace a packet path across subnets
pitfall: Assuming a successful link means IP routing works
pitfall: Ignoring default gateways and route precedence
