id: net-dns-dhcp
title: DNS, DHCP, and Core Network Services
roadmapId: network-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Understand how hosts obtain network configuration and resolve names.
explanation: DHCP can provide addresses and related configuration; DNS maps names to records such as A, AAAA, and CNAME. These services are separate, and failures can look similar to application outages. Use tools such as nslookup or dig to isolate name resolution from connectivity.
codeExample: 
objective: Describe a DHCP lease lifecycle
objective: Inspect common DNS record types
objective: Troubleshoot name-resolution failures
pitfall: Changing DNS records without considering TTL and caching
pitfall: Treating DNS resolution as proof the destination is reachable
