=== TOPIC ===
id: emb-c-firmware
title: C Firmware Structure and Memory Constraints
roadmapId: embedded-systems-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 65
summary: Organize firmware around initialization, main loops, interrupts, and bounded resource use.
explanation: Firmware often has no general-purpose process environment and may use statically allocated buffers. Initialization order, stack size, interrupt context, and memory budgets should be explicit. Dynamic allocation may be unsuitable in some real-time or safety-constrained designs.
codeExample: int main(void) {
    board_init();
    peripherals_init();
    for (;;) {
        poll_inputs();
        update_state();
        service_outputs();
    }
}
objective: Structure startup and main-loop responsibilities
objective: Estimate static RAM and stack usage
objective: Keep interrupt handlers bounded
pitfall: Calling blocking APIs from an interrupt handler without checking constraints
pitfall: Allocating unbounded memory in long-running firmware
prerequisites: emb-mcu-architecture
resource: Barr Group embedded C resources|https://barrgroup.com/embedded-systems|reference
resource: Zephyr Project documentation|https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/|documentation

