id: emb-rtos-scheduling
title: RTOS Tasks, Scheduling, and Interrupts
roadmapId: embedded-systems-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 70
summary: Design firmware tasks around deadlines, priorities, synchronization, and real-time constraints.
explanation: An RTOS provides scheduling and synchronization primitives, but deterministic behavior depends on bounded execution times, interrupt latency, priority design, and resource contention. Meeting average timing is not enough when a deadline is a correctness requirement.
codeExample: 
objective: Define task periods and deadlines
objective: Avoid priority inversion and unbounded blocking
objective: Measure worst-case timing under load
pitfall: Treating a real-time system as merely a fast system
pitfall: Using shared resources without a synchronization strategy
prerequisites: emb-peripherals-buses
resource: FreeRTOS documentation|https://www.freertos.org/Documentation/RTOS_book.html|documentation
resource: Zephyr scheduling documentation|https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/kernel/services/scheduling/index.html|documentation

