id: dso-threat-modeling
title: Threat Modeling for Delivery Pipelines
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Identify how source, build, artifact, and deployment workflows could be abused.
explanation: Threat modeling maps assets, trust boundaries, actors, and attack paths. Build systems and CI credentials are part of the attack surface; protect the integrity and provenance of artifacts that reach production.
codeExample: 
objective: Draw a simple pipeline trust-boundary diagram
objective: Identify high-value credentials and artifacts
objective: Prioritize mitigations by risk
prerequisites: 
resource: OWASP Threat Modeling|https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling|guide
