=== TOPIC ===
id: dso-secure-pipeline
title: Secure CI/CD Pipeline Design
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 60
summary: Apply least privilege, isolated jobs, protected branches, and controlled artifact promotion.
explanation: Pipeline security depends on who can modify workflows, which secrets jobs can access, and how artifacts are built and promoted. Separate untrusted pull-request jobs from privileged release jobs and minimize long-lived credentials.
codeExample: permissions:
  contents: read

# Grant write or deployment permissions only to jobs that require them.
# Keep secrets unavailable to untrusted pull-request workflows.
objective: Restrict permissions for pipeline jobs
objective: Separate build, test, and release trust levels
objective: Require review and provenance for releases
prerequisites: dso-threat-modeling
resource: GitHub Actions security hardening|https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-for-github-actions/security-guides/security-hardening-for-github-actions|documentation
resource: SLSA framework|https://slsa.dev/|framework

=== TOPIC ===
id: dso-sast-dependencies
title: Static Analysis and Dependency Security
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Detect risky code patterns and vulnerable or untrusted dependencies early in development.
explanation: Static analysis, software composition analysis, and dependency review provide different signals. Findings require triage based on reachability, exploitability, exposure, and available fixes; scanner output alone is not a complete risk assessment.
codeExample: 
objective: Add static analysis and dependency checks
objective: Review transitive dependency changes
objective: Triage findings with documented rationale
prerequisites: dso-secure-pipeline
resource: OWASP Dependency-Check|https://owasp.org/www-project-dependency-check/|tool documentation
resource: Semgrep documentation|https://semgrep.dev/docs/|tool documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: dso-secrets-containers
title: Secret Management and Container Hardening
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 60
summary: Reduce credential leakage and harden container images and runtime permissions.
explanation: Secrets should be short-lived where possible, injected through an approved secret manager, and never committed to source. Container hardening includes minimal trusted base images, non-root execution where feasible, pinned artifacts, and runtime restrictions.
codeExample: 
objective: Scan for accidentally committed secrets
objective: Run containers with least privilege
objective: Track image provenance and patching
prerequisites: dso-sast-dependencies
resource: OWASP Secrets Management Cheat Sheet|https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html|guide
resource: Docker security documentation|https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/|documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: dso-iac-policy
title: Infrastructure as Code Security and Policy
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Validate infrastructure definitions before changes are applied.
explanation: Infrastructure as Code makes infrastructure reviewable, but state files, provider credentials, and plan outputs can contain sensitive details. Policy checks should evaluate exposure and configuration constraints before deployment, with exceptions documented and time-bounded.
codeExample: terraform fmt -check
terraform validate
terraform plan -out=tfplan

# Review the plan and policy findings before applying changes.
objective: Review infrastructure plans before apply
objective: Add policy checks for critical misconfigurations
objective: Protect state and provider credentials
prerequisites: dso-secrets-containers
resource: Checkov documentation|https://www.checkov.io/|documentation
resource: Terraform security model|https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/docs|documentation

=== TOPIC ===
id: dso-vulnerability-response
title: Vulnerability Triage and Secure Release Response
roadmapId: devsecops-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 50
summary: Coordinate remediation based on severity, exposure, exploitability, and business context.
explanation: Vulnerability management includes intake, validation, prioritization, remediation, verification, and communication. A patch is not complete until its deployed version and exposure are checked. Exceptions should have an owner, rationale, and expiry.
codeExample: 
objective: Prioritize findings using contextual risk
objective: Verify fixes in the released artifact
objective: Track exceptions and remediation ownership
prerequisites: dso-iac-policy
